# Bounded reconstruction v1

This executable profile addresses MC08–MC12, MC18 and MC26. It constructs a joint
family from declared templates, slots, openings, dated mappings and admitted
observations. It does not discover templates or infer arbitrary company histories.

## Pre-execution research intent and evidence contract

Question: do declared inputs generate the correct family within their finite
scope? Mechanism: rational linear constraints with shared economic identifiers,
explicit finite choices and bounded integer domains. Expected failure modes are
lost dependence, wrong strict endpoints, unexamined rounding and false completeness.
Comparators are an independent Fraction replay/enumerator over original fixtures
and analytic continuous bounds. Exact feasible-set equality and endpoint proofs
are pass criteria. Unsupported operations, unknown backend replies, unfinished
cells or unresolved matching obligations veto exact certification. Corrupted
inputs or protection failures veto acceptance and stop the checker. A numerical
failure triggers repair, not rejection of the research direction. Runtime is
explanatory only. No superiority, general accounting validity, forecast validity,
continuous probabilistic inference or human acceptance follows from these checks.
Conformance JSON and result.md preserve results; progress.md is a reset checkpoint.

Skeptical audit: the earlier ambiguity between named views and search choices is
resolved explicitly below. Baselines use original inputs, not generated expected
answers. Fixture sizes and budgets are engineering choices. No stochastic ranking
or production-default promotion is attempted. A successful command can still be
misleading if both construction and oracle share lowering; the oracle therefore
replays postings independently. The integration checks inspect the unnamed
interior, not only endpoint extrema.

